    title: "Day 7 — The Angel of the Sick",
    category: "novenas",
    day: 7,
    intention: "For the sick and those who care for them",
    text: `O Saint Martin de Porres, who was known as the "Angel of the Sick" because of your tender care for the infirm and dying, I bring before you today all who are suffering from illness of body or soul. You who spent countless hours at the bedsides of the sick, who cleaned their wounds, who fed them, who prayed with them and for them — look upon the sick today with your compassionate gaze. Obtain for them healing according to God's will, relief from their suffering, and the grace to unite their pains to the Passion of Christ. I also pray for all caregivers — doctors, nurses, family members, and friends — who tend to the sick with love and dedication. Give them strength, patience, and perseverance in their noble work. O Saint Martin, angel of the sick, intercede for all who suffer and all who care for them. Amen.`,
