    intention: "To imitate the humble holiness of Saint Martin",
    text: `O glorious Saint Martin de Porres, humble brother, apostle of charity, patron of racial justice and social harmony, you who died on November 3, 1639, and were canonized by Pope John XXIII in 1962 — I honor you today and ask your powerful intercession. Your life was a testament to the truth that holiness is not reserved for the powerful and the privileged, but is available to all who humble themselves before God and serve others with love. You who were called a "mulatto" and treated as inferior by the world were recognized by God as a saint, worthy of the highest glory in heaven. I pray that I may follow your example of humility, charity, and justice. Help me to love God above all things, to serve the poor as I would serve Christ, and to work for a world where every person is recognized as a child of God. O Saint Martin de Porres, humble saint of Peru, glorious brother of the Dominican Order, intercede for me now and at the hour of my death. Amen.`,
